#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ceff3ba-7535-5c2f-87ea-89b1a4c0f528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723470} {:answer/id #uuid "71850664-3d04-51fb-9785-d232bb3818bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723482} {:answer/id #uuid "c050880c-080c-56a6-af99-2dcb03366011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723492} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf809e3-f28c-5c4f-9ec2-0e90d07eb050" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723500} {:answer/id #uuid "f799356d-9fc6-5556-bf9f-7f356c0831e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ceff3ba-7535-5c2f-87ea-89b1a4c0f528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723470} :answer-field/id #uuid "21b0b7f2-d52f-5ffa-a777-a35366eb9101" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "535f00f3-74e5-58c2-a38e-22e5549860f1" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve in $\\mathbb{R}^2$, and let $D$ be the region it encloses. Which of the following vector fields make\n\n$$\n\\oint_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\operatorname{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nfor every such curve?\n\n**I.**\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}_{I}(x,y)=\\begin{pmatrix}x + 2 y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - y\\\\- 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\n**II.**\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}_{II}(x,y)=\\begin{pmatrix}x - \\frac{y}{2} - \\frac{e^{2 y}}{2}\\\\- x e^{2 y} + \\frac{x}{2} + y^{2}\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\n**III.**\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}_{III}(x,y)=\\begin{pmatrix}x^{2} + y^{2} - 2 y \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - y\\\\\\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\end{pmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf{F}=\\langle P,Q\\rangle$. Green's theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\oint_C P\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n=\\iint_D\\left(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nAll the displayed functions have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb{R}^2$. For the circulation to equal area for every such region, the scalar curl must be identically $1$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative.\n\n**I.** \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_y&=2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 1,\\\\\nQ_x&=2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)},\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 1\\right)\\\\\n&=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scalar curl is identically $1$, so select **I**.\n\n**II.** \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_y&=- e^{2 y} - \\frac{1}{2},\\\\\nQ_x&=- e^{2 y} + \\frac{1}{2},\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(- e^{2 y} + \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(- e^{2 y} - \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scalar curl is identically $1$, so select **II**.\n\n**III.** \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_y&=2 y - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 1,\\\\\nQ_x&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)},\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(2 y - 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 1\\right)\\\\\n&=- 2 y + 1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not identically $1$: at $(x,y)=(0,1)$ its value is $-1$. Do not select **III**.\n\nTherefore, select **I and II only**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723497 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a839c19-cf38-5ea9-a908-afb6e909347a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723471} {:answer/id #uuid "3c31e01a-411d-5476-b95c-216562f83c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c31e01a-411d-5476-b95c-216562f83c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723472} :answer-field/id #uuid "2337bee1-c619-5f59-a418-b995f07bb38e" :answer-field/key "**II**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723469} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d281d79-9462-5577-9025-be1ae77283ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723465} {:answer/id #uuid "879b6d20-93a1-53dc-87cb-9e71561b29dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d281d79-9462-5577-9025-be1ae77283ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723465} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fe82200-5ae7-50d1-b750-758905eb49eb" :answer-field/key "**I**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09c68d19-d55f-58aa-925f-dcdab36fddb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723462} {:answer/id #uuid "dff56bf9-db41-5d8f-aef7-00fd981a45f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dff56bf9-db41-5d8f-aef7-00fd981a45f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723499} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f4d8016-e056-5f1c-b015-e7ba2962c96b" :answer-field/key "**III**" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d73866df-233f-51ad-a600-c0df410f8255" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve in $\\mathbb{R}^2$, and let $D$ be the region it encloses. Which of the following vector fields make\n\n$$\n\\oint_C\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\operatorname{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nfor every such curve?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n**I.**\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}_{I}(x,y)=\\begin{pmatrix}- 2 y \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - y + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\\\\\sin{\\left(y \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\n**II.**\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}_{II}(x,y)=\\begin{pmatrix}y - e^{2 y} + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\\\- 2 x e^{2 y} + y\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\n**III.**\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}_{III}(x,y)=\\begin{pmatrix}- \\frac{y}{2} + 2 e^{x + y} + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\\\\\frac{x}{2} + 2 e^{x + y}\\end{pmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf{F}=\\langle P,Q\\rangle$. Green's theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\oint_C P\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n=\\iint_D\\left(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nAll the displayed functions have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb{R}^2$. For the circulation to equal area for every such region, the scalar curl must be identically $1$. Hold the other coordinate constant in each partial derivative.\n\n**I.** \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_y&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 1,\\\\\nQ_x&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)},\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} - 1\\right)\\\\\n&=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scalar curl is identically $1$, so select **I**.\n\n**II.** \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_y&=- 2 e^{2 y} + 1,\\\\\nQ_x&=- 2 e^{2 y},\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(- 2 e^{2 y}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(- 2 e^{2 y} + 1\\right)\\\\\n&=-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not identically $1$: at $(x,y)=(0,0)$ its value is $-1$. Do not select **II**.\n\n**III.** \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_y&=2 e^{x + y} - \\frac{1}{2},\\\\\nQ_x&=2 e^{x + y} + \\frac{1}{2},\\\\\nQ_x-P_y&=\\left(2 e^{x + y} + \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad-\\left(2 e^{x + y} - \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scalar curl is identically $1$, so select **III**.\n\nTherefore, select **I and III only**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723562 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Check both the specified field and the orientation sign." :answer/id #uuid "0a87197e-aaa7-55b9-b62f-1dc780195cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723564} {:answer/feedback "Correct: substitute the field, differentiate and apply the traversal sign." :answer/id #uuid "489eafd5-72ff-5182-a96a-fe566384293c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723573} {:answer/feedback "Use the specified field; the other unit-curl field gives a different pointwise integrand." :answer/id #uuid "52b7236e-6ec7-5478-bd66-156eddb78449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723577} {:answer/feedback "The surviving field component must be evaluated at the correct coordinate." :answer/id #uuid "7850724b-1f08-5210-bf0a-280c06bc8f88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 3 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723583} {:answer/feedback "The surviving field component must be evaluated at the correct coordinate." :answer/id #uuid "d80ec89f-965a-53dd-8f8b-3ce270ea542e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: substitute the field, differentiate and apply the traversal sign." :answer/id #uuid "489eafd5-72ff-5182-a96a-fe566384293c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723573} :answer-field/id #uuid "67b30410-1fb4-5ef9-9e38-2b736ac1bdf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "037cbf48-5375-54ff-af91-4db1803c121c" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa427c6b7ece0f686452452cdac619cda3d8a55fc7574d2772bf7462468d6d99.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by $C$, with\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}, 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 3 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\rangle.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\le t\\le \\frac{5 \\pi}{3}.\n$$\n\nUse $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x$. Determine the **pointwise integrand** obtained from this field and parametrization, with the sign adjusted for orientation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Area}(D)=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{3}}\\boxed{\\ ?\\ }\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDo not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "The scalar curl is $1-0=1$. The boundary is positively oriented, so we use its circulation without an extra minus sign.\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Area}(D)=\\oint_C(P\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y)=\\oint_C x\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)=\\langle - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}, 3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\rangle.\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the surviving field component, including the orientation sign, and multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=x(t)y^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&=\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the missing pointwise expression is $\\left(\\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Use the coordinate derivative, not the coordinate itself." :answer/id #uuid "453345c9-a4cf-5499-b390-eda1ee28da15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(12 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723571} {:answer/feedback "Use the specified field; the other unit-curl field gives a different pointwise integrand." :answer/id #uuid "48c9a003-c44c-518f-9587-acd7543d4a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 12 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723574} {:answer/feedback "Multiply the derivative by the substituted field component, including its sign." :answer/id #uuid "a887d40b-114f-56ac-9b95-ee976def5a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723586} {:answer/feedback "The surviving field component must be evaluated at the correct coordinate." :answer/id #uuid "c47bcad1-8867-5e4f-b8ac-f16547a8b1a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723590} {:answer/feedback "Correct: substitute the field, differentiate and apply the traversal sign." :answer/id #uuid "fc26d6e4-ff4e-5c61-9ae6-41a9ed58947a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(12 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: substitute the field, differentiate and apply the traversal sign." :answer/id #uuid "fc26d6e4-ff4e-5c61-9ae6-41a9ed58947a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(12 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723595} :answer-field/id #uuid "be8de9ce-dcde-5673-bdec-7d6e7532548e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04b0aacd-804e-59ed-98e0-9e020a7d4da6" :question/problem "![](images/bc/bc75ddae3094fd68394735ab7684151688cc347239196bd6391fb7a306163bf4.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by $C$, with\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 12 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}, 6 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\rangle.\n$$\n\n$$\n0\\le t\\le 2 \\pi.\n$$\n\nUse $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x$. Determine the **pointwise integrand** obtained from this field and parametrization, with the sign adjusted for orientation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Area}(D)=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\boxed{\\ ?\\ }\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDo not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "The scalar curl is $1-0=1$. The boundary is positively oriented, so we use its circulation without an extra minus sign.\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Area}(D)=\\oint_C(P\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y)=\\oint_C x\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)=\\langle - 12 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 12 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}, 6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\rangle.\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the surviving field component, including the orientation sign, and multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=x(t)y^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=\\left(6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(12 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&=\\left(6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(12 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the missing pointwise expression is $\\left(6 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(12 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Correct: substitute the field, differentiate and apply the traversal sign." :answer/id #uuid "1eb835e0-5e76-5500-a19e-f8744a82742d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723567} {:answer/feedback "Use the specified field; the other unit-curl field gives a different pointwise integrand." :answer/id #uuid "4d098bd2-aec3-5d3a-b3da-1f50049e4596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 3 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723575} {:answer/feedback "Multiply the derivative by the substituted field component, including its sign." :answer/id #uuid "729015cd-ea0f-5635-b505-bd91d4993ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723581} {:answer/feedback "Apply the differentiated coordinate scale once, not twice." :answer/id #uuid "73a92ede-b7aa-51f6-a5c0-a9ae1f40108a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723582} {:answer/feedback "Keep the scale of the substituted coordinate." :answer/id #uuid "eba905bc-b5a7-5a2f-aedd-7c3e8a34b626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: substitute the field, differentiate and apply the traversal sign." :answer/id #uuid "1eb835e0-5e76-5500-a19e-f8744a82742d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723567} :answer-field/id #uuid "309cb293-d7ed-5100-946a-4d2ff8ec1130" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723569}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51978717-99b3-5800-b393-016db3ffecb9" :question/problem "![](images/86/86ce51e0ca19867f08bb53d0d61acc330e892e34e5335eb14cea6241b8a618b8.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by $C$, with\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 3 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 3 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}, 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\rangle.\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\le t\\le \\frac{5 \\pi}{3}.\n$$\n\nUse $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0$. Determine the **pointwise integrand** obtained from this field and parametrization, with the sign adjusted for orientation:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Area}(D)=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}^{\\frac{5 \\pi}{3}}\\boxed{\\ ?\\ }\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nDo not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "The scalar curl is $0-(-1)=1$. The boundary is positively oriented, so we use its circulation without an extra minus sign.\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Area}(D)=\\oint_C(P\\,\\mathrm{d}x+Q\\,\\mathrm{d}y)=\\oint_C -y\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r^{\\prime}(t)=\\langle - 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}, 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\rangle.\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the surviving field component, including the orientation sign, and multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)&=-y(t)x^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)\\\\&=\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the missing pointwise expression is $\\left(- 3 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186723578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Use the specified field; the other unit-curl field gives a different pointwise integrand." :answer/id #uuid "14999ec5-d273-55a4-abb3-6e3132710f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723565} {:answer/feedback "Check both the specified field and the orientation sign." :answer/id #uuid "1840b5d8-47fd-58d1-a5e5-539a2e08c348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right) \\left(4 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723566} {:answer/feedback "Correct: substitute the field, differentiate and apply the traversal sign." :answer/id 